stolic pressures is known as pulse pressure, while the average pressure during a cardiac cycle is known as mean arterial pressure.","typeGUID":"b34a64b9-554a-42b1-8f8a-7d5c2339f9c4","typeName":"string"},"displayName":{"class":"PrimitivePropertyValue","headerVersion":1,"instancePropertyCategory":"PRIMITIVE","primitiveDefCategory":"OM_PRIMITIVE_TYPE_STRING","primitiveValue":"Patient Blood Pressure","typeGUID":"b34a64b9-554a-42b1-8f8a-7d5c2339f9c4","typeName":"string"},"qualifiedName":{"class":"PrimitivePropertyValue","headerVersion":1,"instancePropertyCategory":"PRIMITIVE","primitiveDefCategory":"OM_PRIMITIVE_TYPE_STRING","primitiveValue":"GlossaryTerm::ClinicalTrialTerminology::PatientBloodPressure","typeGUID":"b34a64b9-554a-42b1-8f8a-7d5c2339f9c4","typeName":"string"},"summary":{"class":"PrimitivePropertyValue","headerVersion":1,"instancePropertyCategory":"PRIMITIVE","primitiveDefCategory":"OM_PRIMITIVE_TYPE_STRING","primitiveValue":"Blood pressure of patient (systolic and diastolic).","typeGUID":"b34a64b9-554a-42b1-8f8a-7d5c2339f9c4","typeName":"string"},"usage":{"class":"PrimitivePropertyValue","headerVersion":1,"instancePropertyCategory":"PRIMITIVE","primitiveDefCategory":"OM_PRIMITIVE_TYPE_STRING","primitiveValue":"Acts as one of the standard mechanism for measuring the health of a patient in a clinical trial.","typeGUID":"b34a64b9-554a-42b1-8f8a-7d5c2339f9c4","typeName":"string"},"versionIdentifier":{"class":"PrimitivePropertyValue","headerVersion":1,"instancePropertyCategory":"PRIMITIVE","primitiveDefCategory":"OM_PRIMITIVE_TYPE_STRING","primitiveValue":"6.3-SNAPSHOT","typeGUID":"b34a64b9-554a-42b1-8f8a-7d5c2339f9c4","typeName":"string"}}},"status":"ACTIVE","type":{"class":"InstanceType","headerVersion":1,"typeDefCategory":"ENTITY_DEF","typeDefGUID":"0db3e6ec-f5ef-4d75-ae38-b7ee6fd6ec0a","typeDefName":"GlossaryTerm","typeDefVersion":1},"updateTime":1639984840038,"updatedBy":"Egeria Project","version":1791274688680},{"class":"EntityDetail","classifications":[{"